{
    "background_story": "Raylan was a flamboyant and charismatic 18th-century aristocrat known for his extravagant fashion sense. He was particularly famous for his elaborate perukes, which he wore to every high-society gathering. His favorite was a towering white wig adorned with sparkling silver threads and a sprinkle of diamond dust. Raylan's perukes were not just a statement piece, but an extension of his personality - bold, daring, and unapologetic. He would often change his wig to match his mood, donning a more subdued style for somber occasions and a vibrant red one for masquerade balls. Raylan's love of perukes earned him the nickname 'The Wigged Wonder' among the aristocracy, and his legendary style continues to inspire fashion enthusiasts to this day.",
